Here are two other tricks to make sure you survive:
* If you starve to death while wearing an amulet of life saving, you'll
fill your stomach. This breaks no in-game conducts, so is a pretty good
solution if you're doing foodless atheist or something. You want to
starve in a locked closet, otherwise something may kill you're
fainting. If that happens, you'll activate your amulet, but you'll fill
your HP, not your stomach, and you'll probably starve to death soon
after. (or get killed for real by whatever killed you in the first
place)
* If you polymorph yourself, you'll fill your stomach. This breaks the
polyself conduct only if you polymorph into something other than your
original race. So if you're a human and polyself into a human, you fill
your stomach without breaking the polyself conduct. Foodless games that
don't use this loophole are considered "true polyselfless"

